Messaging System – Profile Header Status

This feature updates the profile header in the messaging system so that the active/inactive status is no longer hardcoded. Instead, the status dynamically reflects whether the other user is currently online.

Presence Tracking: When a user logs into the messaging app or becomes active, their status updates to Online. When they log out, close the app, or become inactive, their status updates to Offline or Away.

Real-Time Updates: The status is updated in real time so that other users immediately see whether someone is available.

Profile Header Integration: The status is displayed directly below the user’s name and email in the profile header, with a green dot for “Online” and a gray dot for “Offline.”

Extension Sidebar (Messaging Section): The same active/inactive status is displayed in the extension sidebar under the messaging section, so availability is visible across both the profile header and the sidebar.